# Both AI tools (deck evaluator + website reviewer) call Google's Gemini
# directly through the open-source Vercel AI SDK's Google provider
# (lib/ai.ts, @ai-sdk/google, model "gemini-flash-latest"). Gemini's Flash
# tier has a genuine no-credit-card-required free quota, unlike the
# Anthropic API (no standing free tier -- it rejects requests once trial
# credits run out, which is what this app hit before switching).
#
# Get a free key from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# (no credit card required). Set it below for local dev, and directly in
# the Vercel dashboard (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables,
# Production environment) for deploys -- never paste a real key into a
# chat, a commit, or any file with a real value in it.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# Required outside Vercel (local dev, this sandbox, or any other host):
# point this at a real Chromium binary. Install one locally with
# `npx playwright install chromium`, then set this to the path it reports.
# On Vercel, leave this unset -- lib/screenshot.ts detects the VERCEL env var
# (set automatically by the platform) and uses @sparticuz/chromium instead.
PLAYWRIGHT_EXECUTABLE_PATH=
